49.0.1.840.0.afa36fda4801b3fe5585239b298faad267b95141.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 13 at 2:53PM MDT until August 13 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...East Central Jefferson County in central Colorado...\nWest Central Arapahoe County in northeastern Colorado...\nSouthwestern Denver County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 600 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 253 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. Minor flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly in the advisory area. Up to\n0.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSouthwestern Denver, Lakewood, northeastern Littleton, Englewood,\nGreenwood Village, Sheridan, Morrison, Red Rocks Park, Tiny Town,\nIdledale, Indian Hills, Cherry Hills Village, Columbine, Ken\nCaryl and Genesee.","ends":"2026-08-13T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Arapahoe, CO; Denver, CO; Jefferson, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6d07ca20bb422e3e2435f7c4b83408d8a105c29c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6d07ca20bb422e3e2435f7c4b83408d8a105c29c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-13T19:21:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 131921 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 121 PM MDT Thu Aug 13 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Localized flash flooding possible due to heavy rain producing thunderstorms. Highest risk is over the eastern Colorado plains, where a Flood Watch is in effect from 3 pm to 10 pm. - Another round of storms Friday afternoon/evening with a continued threat o","url":"https://forecast.weath